-- title:
--   Set Integral Factorization Under Independence
-- statement:
--   Let $m\leq m_\Omega$ be measurable spaces on a probability space $(\Omega,P)$. Let $X:\Omega\to\mathcal X$ be measurable, where $\mathcal X$ is a topological measurable Borel space, and assume the sigma-algebra $m$ is independent of the comap sigma-algebra generated by $X$. If $A$ is measurable in $m$ and $f:\mathcal X\to\mathbb R$ is bounded continuous, then
--
--   $$\int_A f(X(\omega))\,dP(\omega)=(P(A)).\operatorname{toReal}\,\int_\Omega f(X(\omega))\,dP(\omega).$$
--
--   The conclusion uses the real coercion `toReal` of the probability $P(A)$. This is a reusable factorization identity for independent events and bounded observables.
--
